 "en": [
  {
   "title": "Creative Forge",
   "icon": "industrialfurnace:forge_controller",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "text": "The Creative Forge is the endgame multiblock of Molten Industry: a 7×7×7 machine that forges creative items from top-tier materials of other mods, a fluid and a huge amount of energy."
    },
    {
     "items": [
      "industrialfurnace:forge_controller",
      "industrialfurnace:forge_core",
      "industrialfurnace:forge_frame",
      "industrialfurnace:forge_casing",
      "industrialfurnace:forge_vent",
      "industrialfurnace:forge_glass",
      "industrialfurnace:forge_input_port",
      "industrialfurnace:forge_output_port",
      "industrialfurnace:forge_energy_port",
      "industrialfurnace:forge_builder",
      "industrialfurnace:forge_speed_module"
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Structure"
    },
    {
     "text": "1. A 7×7×7 cube, hollow inside, with the Forge Core exactly in the centre."
    },
    {
     "text": "2. All edges and corners are Forge Frame."
    },
    {
     "text": "3. The faces are Forge Casing, Vent, Glass or ports, in any mix."
    },
    {
     "text": "4. The controller goes in the middle of the bottom row of a face, one block above the frame."
    },
    {
     "text": "5. You need at least one Input Port, one Output Port and one Energy Port anywhere in the faces."
    },
    {
     "text": "The controller screen shows the coordinates of the first wrong block. With EMI, the Creative Forge Structure page shows the whole build layer by layer."
    },
    {
     "heading": "Reference build"
    },
    {
     "table": [
      [
       "Forge Frame",
       "68"
      ],
      [
       "Forge Casing",
       "97"
      ],
      [
       "Forge Glass",
       "36 (3×3 windows on the front, sides and roof)"
      ],
      [
       "Forge Vent",
       "10"
      ],
      [
       "Ports",
       "2 energy (next to the controller), 2 input (right side), 2 output (left side)"
      ],
      [
       "Controller and Core",
       "1 each"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "Casing, vents and glass are interchangeable, so the layout is only a suggestion."
    },
    {
     "heading": "Forge Builder"
    },
    {
     "text": "Place the controller, then right-click it with the Forge Builder: the whole forge appears at once. The blocks are taken from your inventory (free in creative mode); if something is missing, the chat lists what. The builder never breaks foreign blocks: if one is in the way, it tells you its coordinates."
    },
    {
     "heading": "Ports"
    },
    {
     "table": [
      [
       "Input Port",
       "18 slots and a 512,000 mB tank. Fill it with pipes, hoppers or by hand."
      ],
      [
       "Output Port",
       "18 slots. Pushes finished items into adjacent chests and pipes twice a second."
      ],
      [
       "Energy Port",
       "Takes FE/RF from any cable into the controller's 50 billion FE buffer."
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Forging"
    },
    {
     "text": "As soon as the input ports hold all items and the fluid of a recipe, the forge takes them and starts. The energy is spent evenly over the whole craft; if there is not enough, the forge pauses and resumes when power returns. If the output ports are full, the finished item waits inside."
    },
    {
     "text": "Breaking the controller mid-craft drops the ingredients it has already taken, so nothing is lost."
    },
    {
     "heading": "Speed modules"
    },
    {
     "text": "Up to 4 Forge Speed Modules fit on the roof pylons: right-click the roof under a pylon. Each module adds +1 to the crafting speed (4 modules = 5× speed); energy per tick grows the same way, so a craft costs the same. Shift + right-click with an empty hand takes a module off."
    },
    {
     "heading": "What it forges"
    },
    {
     "text": "Recipes appear only when the needed mods are installed (Mekanism, Avaritia, Draconic Evolution, AE2). Change them with a datapack or KubeJS: recipe type industrialfurnace:forging."
    },
